 DemoNew connected;f
⍝ ⎕NEW-style GUI code running on EWC: written as for ⎕NEW, with ⎕NEW→eNEW and
⍝ ⎕WG/⎕WS→eWG/eWS as the only changes. Objects are unnamed refs; children are
⍝ made by running eNEW inside the parent; the onSelect callback gets a ref.
 EWC.CONNECTED←connected
 eEX'Form'eWN⍕⎕THIS ⍝ Close the menu form (other demos replace it by reusing F1)

 f←eNEW'Form'(('Caption' 'eNEW')('Posn'(50 50))('Size'(140 460))('Coord' 'Pixel'))
 f.Name←f.eNEW'Edit'(('Text' 'World')('Posn'(20 20))('Size'(23 190)))
 f.(Greet←eNEW'Button'(('Caption' 'Greet')('Posn'(20 220))('Size'(23 90))('Event'('onSelect' 'CBNew'))))
 f.(Out←eNEW'Label'(('Caption' 'Press Greet')('Posn'(60 20))('Size'(23 290))))

 F1←f ⍝ The demo menu is added to F1
